  "entryMissionDorAnsia03Title": "The Lord is my shepherd",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04CentralInsight": "The bread is for today",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04HookNote": "Jesus teaches asking for the day — not the stockpile. The Kingdom comes before the bread.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04Intro": "Asking for daily bread is the opposite of anticipating the whole month.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04Objective": "Pray the day, not the census of fear.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04Title": "Our Father",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05CentralInsight": "The inheritance is kept",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05HookNote": "Hope does not deny suffering. It anchors it in the resurrection. Continue in the Sermon on the Mount.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05Intro": "Peter anchors sufferers in a kept inheritance — then, the canon.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05Objective": "Leave the pain trail for the curriculum: Sermon on the Mount.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05Title": "Living hope",
  "entryMissionDorRecome01CentralInsight": "God still asks where you are",
  "entryMissionDorRecome01HookNote": "The first move after the fall is God seeking — not the human hiding successfully.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome01Intro": "Distrust breaks communion — and still God asks.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome01Objective": "See the fall as a break, not the end of the conversation.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome01Title": "The fall",
  "entryMissionDorRecome02CentralInsight": "There is a seed after the door",
  "entryMissionDorRecome02EchoQuestion": "He asked. And after the answer, did the story end?",
  "entryMissionDorRecome02HookNote": "In the same chapter as the expulsion, God speaks of a seed. Judgment does not cancel the story.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome02Intro": "Sin has a cost. The promise does not vanish.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome02Objective": "Read consequence and promise in the same text.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome02Title": "Consequences",
  "entryMissionDorRecome03CentralInsight": "A fresh start is covenant, not erasing",
  "entryMissionDorRecome03EchoQuestion": "There is a seed after the door. Does the world start again by erasing the past?",
  "entryMissionDorRecome03HookNote": "The world starts again under covenant, not amnesia. The bow reminds God — and us.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome03Intro": "Judgment and a fresh start fit in the same God.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome03Objective": "See the flood as judgment that keeps a remnant.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome03Title": "Flood",
  "entryMissionDorRecome04CentralInsight": "A fresh start walks outward",
  "entryMissionDorRecome04EchoQuestion": "A fresh start is covenant. Is Babel fixed with another tower?",
  "entryMissionDorRecome04HookNote": "God does not fix Babel with another tower. He calls a family to be a blessing.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome04Intro": "Leaving the land is the fresh-start gesture that blesses others.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome04Objective": "Link a fresh start to a call, not to isolation.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome04Title": "Abram's call",
  "entryMissionDorRecome05CentralInsight": "There is comfort for those who truly mourn",
  "entryMissionDorRecome05EchoQuestion": "A fresh start walks outward. Those who mourn what died find what in the Kingdom?",
  "entryMissionDorRecome05HookNote": "The Kingdom does not rush grief. It comforts. The canonical trail begins in Genesis 1–11.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome05Intro": "Those who mourn what died are blessed. Continue in Genesis 1–11.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome05Objective": "Leave the pain trail for the curriculum: Genesis 1–11.",
  "entryMissionDorRecome05Title": "Those who mourn",
  "entryTrailAnsiedadeDescription": "Five scenes to cast tomorrow on the Father — then continue in the canon.",
